  {
   "id": "b4l",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1222,
   "y": 550,
   "width": 108,
   "height": 15,
   "strokeColor": "#b91c1c",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100051,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700357,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "2PC, or a saga",
   "originalText": "2PC, or a saga",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "ren",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 686,
   "width": 1019,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100052,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700364,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Creating a reservation and decrementing inventory MUST BE ATOMIC. Split across two services with two databases, there is no\ntransaction that covers both - so you need 2PC (blocking, lock-holding) or a saga with compensation (eventually consistent,\nmeaning a window in which inventory says a room is free and a reservation for it already exists). BOTH TRADE CORRECTNESS FOR A\nDISTRIBUTION YOU DO NOT NEED AT 3 RESERVATIONS/SEC.",
   "originalText": "Creating a reservation and decrementing inventory MUST BE ATOMIC. Split across two services with two databases, there is no\ntransaction that covers both - so you need 2PC (blocking, lock-holding) or a saga with compensation (eventually consistent,\nmeaning a window in which inventory says a room is free and a reservation for it already exists). BOTH TRADE CORRECTNESS FOR A\nDISTRIBUTION YOU DO NOT NEED AT 3 RESERVATIONS/SEC.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "ren2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 764,
   "width": 1019,
   "height": 48,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100053,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700371,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "When WOULD you split them? If inventory reads became hot enough to need independent scaling - the Booking.com-scale scenario.\nEven then the better first move is a read replica or a cache, not a service boundary, because the WRITE path is what needs the\ntransaction and the write path is tiny.",
   "originalText": "When WOULD you split them? If inventory reads became hot enough to need independent scaling - the Booking.com-scale scenario.\nEven then the better first move is a read replica or a cache, not a service boundary, because the WRITE path is what needs the\ntransaction and the write path is tiny.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
